    "text": "**Case A**\n\n- **A1 \u2013 Yes.** The seven-day search of the key's requests returned only the stable single-region traffic, so nothing anomalous precedes the burst. This treats the burst as misuse, which the evidence strongly suggests but does not strictly prove.\n- **A2 \u2013 Yes.** The burst and the payout changes happened at 19 minutes and the check scored the account at 30 minutes, so the evidence already existed when it ran. This assumes the check had access to request and account-change data.\n- **A3 \u2013 No, not by itself.** A shared payout destination fits one owner, but it equally fits a mule destination used across several compromised accounts.\n- **A4 \u2013 Yes, weakly.** A real owner whose payouts were diverted would probably have complained within 30 days, so silence is some evidence. It is weak because reports can lag and nothing indicates anyone looked.\n- **A5 \u2013 Yes.** A new proxy and fingerprint minutes after publication, combined with a webhook, a new payout destination and a faster schedule, clearly warrants investigation.\n\n**Case B**\n\n- **B1 \u2013 Yes.** Each account has 100 transactions, so D's 0 percent is lower than the 2 percent at A, B and C (the difference is small in absolute terms).\n- **B2 \u2013 No.** A combined figure says nothing about each account; if the accounts differ at all, at least one is above 5 percent.\n- **B3 \u2013 Yes.** The search covered all merchant accounts and found only A and the closed account. It would not catch accounts held under another identity or a nominee.\n- **B4 \u2013 Cannot tell.** Different analysts on different days does not establish independence; both may have looked at the same templates and data, or the second may have read the first note.\n- **B5 \u2013 No.** A payment blocked as suspected fraud never completed, so it could not produce a chargeback; the missing chargeback is not evidence that it was clean.\n- **B6 \u2013 Yes.** Shared templates, a common descriptor pattern, settlement through the same four accounts and the link to a rejected application are enough to investigate them together.\n\nRESULT CF-081 | A1: Yes | A2: Yes | A3: No, not by itself | A4: Yes, weakly | A5: Yes | B1: Yes | B2: No | B3: Yes | B4: Cannot tell | B5: No | B6: Yes"
